<Base title="About | TOW ARCHIVE">
  <section class="about-simple" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <h1 id="about-heading" class="sr-only">About</h1>
    <p>TOW ARCHIVE is a personal and evolving research archive, created and curated by Tow Lichuan Deng. It brings together encounters with contemporary art, observations, and questions that continue beyond the moment of viewing.</p>
    <p>Exhibition Notes records exhibitions and artistic encounters from a situated, personal perspective. These notes are neither comprehensive reviews nor definitive judgements; they are traces of looking, thinking, and returning.</p>
    <p>People, Institutions, and Concepts form interconnected indexes across the archive. Rather than presenting a fixed map of the art world, they follow relationships between artistic practices, places, organisations, and ideas as they emerge and change.</p>
    <p>My interests centre on curatorial practices, site-specific and public art, and the ways institutions shape the circulation and interpretation of art. Translation, across contexts as well as languages, runs through these inquiries.</p>
    <p>Moving between Chinese, Japanese, and English, the archive remains partial, subjective, and open to revision. It is both a record of where I have been and a way of asking where to look next.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
